# Zhaozhou C++ format law (charter 27 "format" tier, review M1).
#
# Base Google (2-space, 80-col heritage) widened to 100 columns because the
# frozen numeric laws and identifier-heavy fixed-point lines legitimately run
# long; include sorting OFF (order carries the generated-before-consumer and
# spec-citation conventions). This file was chosen to MINIMIZE reformat churn
# against the hand-written tree (measured: ~2.9k changed lines vs ~7.2k for a
# 4-space LLVM base) — the one-time mechanical reformat lives in its own
# commit so blame/grief stays attributable.
#
# Scope (the tier checks exactly this): reference/, tests/, tools/capture
# C/C++ sources EXCEPT generated files (reference/include/zref/generated/ is
# fixgen-owned byte-identity evidence; runtime/include/zhao_abi.h lives
# outside the swept dirs and is abi-gen-owned). Verify with:
#   npx -y clang-format@1.8.0 --dry-run --Werror <files>   (LLVM 15)
# The npm package pin keeps local and CI checks on the SAME clang-format
# major version (runner-distro clang-format drifts).
---
BasedOnStyle: Google
ColumnLimit: 100
SortIncludes: Never
